dShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-22T16:56:15Z","updated_at":"2025-10-22T16:58:02Z","body":"This doesn't seem like a bug, non-uniform scales for bodies is not supported, Jolt just makes this explicit, and Jolt does not support this, it isn't that the scale is too high, it's that it's not uniform, as you can see by it replacing the scale with a uniform one\n\nAs Jolt doesn't support non-uniform scale, the solution is to fix this, the message shouldn't be ignored\n\nSee the documentation note:\n> With a non-uniform scale, this node will likely not behave as expected. It is advised to keep its scale the same on all axes and adjust its collision shape(s) instead.\n\nAlso the configuration warning that pops up in the editor if you set the scale in a non-uniform way:\n> With a non-uniform scale this node will probably not function as expected.\n> Please make its scale uniform (i.e. the same on all axes), and change the size in children collision shapes instead.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"